sa-3-p2 = prose (cons "For a source-free electromagnetic field in units \(c=1\), define \(F:=E+iB\). Maxwell's evolution equations \(\partial_tE=\nabla\times B\), \(\partial_tB=-\nabla\times E\) give, by direct substitution," (cons "\[" (cons "i\partial_tF=i(\nabla\times B-i\nabla\times E)" (cons "=\nabla\times(E+iB)=\nabla\times F." (cons "\tag{A.9}" (cons "\]" (cons "The constraints \(\nabla\cdot E=\nabla\cdot B=0\) combine as \(\nabla\cdot F=0\). The displayed equation is the complex form of source-free Maxwell evolution ([72](#ref-72)); the Riemann–Silberstein/photon-wave-function representation has an established treatment in Bialynicki-Birula ([73](#ref-73)). It is an exact algebraic change of representation of the same field equations." nil)))))))
